[{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find the resultant force in each of the following cases, stating both the value and direction:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q1a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q1b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>15 N upwards</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>7 N left</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Given that each of these particles is stationary, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q2a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q2b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q2c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q2d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 2</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 6</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>+ 4 = 38 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\" data-display=\"false\"></span><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 34</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>40 + <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\" data-display=\"false\"></span><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 20</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that the object is at rest.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q3a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q3b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q3c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 62 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 31</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>16 + <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>3 = 40 so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 27  12 + 4 = 2<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 8</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 12 so 3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 12 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\" data-display=\"false\"></span><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 4</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Each of the following diagrams shows an object acted on by a set of forces. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that the object is moving with constant velocity.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q4a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q4b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 2<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>+ 4, 10 = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>+ <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>   So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 8, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 2</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>7 = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>+ 2<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, 12 = 2<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>+ 3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>   <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 3, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 2</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>An object of weight 50 N is hanging by a string in equilibrium as shown in the diagram.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/questions/assets/diagrams/q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>By using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the mass of the object.</p></li></ol><p>The string snaps and the object drops.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>State the size and direction of the resultant force acting on the object.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 50N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>50 = 10<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 5 kg</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>50 N downwards</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>State the weight of an object of mass 50 kg</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>on earth given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.81\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>on the moon given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=1.63\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 50 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.81 = 490.5 N  491 N (3 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 50 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 1.63 = 81.5 N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>An object has weight 4000 N on Earth where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the weight of the same object on the moon where the acceleration due to gravity is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>4000 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\div\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.8 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 1.6 = 653 N (3 SF)  650 N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>An object of mass 0.4 kg is being held in equilibrium by an upwards force of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the weight of the object.</p></li><li><p>Hence, state the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The upwards force is removed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>State the size and direction of the resultant force acting on the object.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>0.4 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.8 = 3.92 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>= 3.92</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>3.92 N downwards</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A small body is hanging in equilibrium at the end of a vertical string.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Draw a force diagram to represent the forces acting on the body.</p></li></ol><p>Find, using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>weight of the body if the mass is 2 kg.</p></li><li><p>mass of the body if its weight is 34.3 N.</p></li><li><p>tension in the string if the mass is 0.5 kg.</p></li><li><p>tension in the string if the weight of the body is 14.7 N.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/solutions/assets/diagrams/s9a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>2 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.8 = 19.6 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>34.3 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\div\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.8 = 3.5 kg</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>0.5 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 9.8 = 4.9 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>14.7 N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A box is at rest on a horizontal table.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Draw a force diagram to represent the forces acting on the box.</p></li></ol><p>Find, using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>weight of the box if the box is 1.5 kg.</p></li><li><p>mass of the box if its weight is 60 N.</p></li><li><p>mass of the box if the normal reaction of the table on the box is 5 N.</p></li><li><p>normal reaction of the table on the box if the mass of the box is 1.2 kg.</p></li><li><p>normal reaction of the table on the box if the weight of the body is 25 N.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/solutions/assets/diagrams/s10a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>1.5 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 10 = 15 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>60 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\div\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 10 = 6 kg</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>5 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\div\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 10 = 0.5 kg</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>1.2 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> 10 = 12 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p>25 N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.66-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A book of mass 400 g is being pushed along with a force of 2 N on a smooth horizontal table.</p><p>Draw a force diagram to represent the forces acting on the book.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.66/solutions/assets/diagrams/s11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]}]